// Probes whether comparisons inside `previous within` are evaluated at
// the prior tp (correct) or the current tp (wrong). The body refers to
// `context.input.amount` whose semantics under Lean dictate which tp's
// binding is consulted. DSQL might apply the comparison at the current
// tp instead.

permit (
    principal,
    action == Drupe::Action::"Transfer",
    resource
)
when temporal {
    previous within 5s (Drupe::Action::"Transfer"::request{ input.user: context.input.user } && context.input.amount > 100)
};
